# Resident idle local-mining cycle. Location POIs resolve from live state.
# refuel FIRST, while still docked from the prior cycle: it tops the tank up
# before each trip AND recovers a bot that has run itself to empty. A trailing
# refuel can't do that — an empty bot can't undock to reach it.
#
# 25 -> 100 on 2026-08-21. 25 was a hard cap that fired long before the hold
# filled: across ~1,100 mine actions each, miner-1/miner-4/miner-9/random-clark
# filled the hull ZERO times and hauled a partial load back every cycle, while
# the three agents on `loop -f 100` per-agent scripts were stopping naturally on
# cargo_full. The count is not a target — `mine` + cargo_full raises a
# GoalReachedError the loop treats as a positive early exit, so 100 means "mine
# until full". On a healthy belt the hull fills in ~15 cycles (operator), so the
# higher ceiling only bites near depletion, where `-f` is tolerating misses
# anyway and the extra attempts are what earn the load.
refuel
undock
travel $ASTEROID_BELT$
loop -f 100 mine
travel $STATION$
dock
deposit_all
